# .gitignore
#
# Ordered by what it is protecting against, most serious first.

# --- credentials: the entries that matter -----------------------------------------------
# Nothing here is recoverable once committed. Git history is the one place a secret cannot
# be deleted from, which is why scripts/check-secrets.sh runs on every push as well —
# .gitignore prevents the accident, the scan catches the one that got past it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# .env.dev is the shared local-development variable set (see its header). It carries no
# credential material — only the well-known local-stack password that config/dev.yaml and
# deploy/docker-compose.dev.yml already use — and every `make run-*` target sources it, so
# it has to be in the repository or the targets work only for whoever wrote them.
!.env.dev

# Local development scratch: the dev issuer's key and the ids dev-up.sh discovers.
.dev/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
credentials.json
service-account*.json
kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig
.aws/
.netrc
!testdata/**/*.pem

# --- terraform state: credentials by another name ----------------------------------------
# tfstate contains every resource attribute, including generated passwords and connection
# strings, in plaintext. State lives in the S3 backend (deployment.md §2), never in git.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
crash.log
crash.*.log
*.tfplan
*.tfvars
!example.tfvars
!*.auto.tfvars.example

# --- build output ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/bin/
/dist/
/build/
/out/
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# --- test and profiling artifacts ------------------------------------------------------------
*.test
*.out
coverage.out
coverage.html
coverage-*.out
cover.out
*.prof
*.cpu
*.mem
*.trace
# testify/rapid failure archives: reproducible from the seed, not worth versioning
.rapid/
/testdata/fuzz/

# --- tooling artifacts ------------------------------------------------------------------------
.loadtest/
evidence/
/sbom/
*.cyclonedx.json
*.spdx.json
.golangci-cache/
.gocache/

# --- local stack ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The postgres binary that appears at the repo root on some local setups: a 4 MB artifact
# nobody meant to commit.
/postgres
/redis-server
docker-compose.override.yml

# --- editors and OS ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.shared.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- language tooling -------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- deliberately NOT ignored -------------------------------------------------------------------
# go.sum          — the integrity record; ignoring it defeats module verification entirely
# .golangci.yml   — the lint configuration is part of the contract, not a local preference
# scripts/secrets-allowlist.txt — hashes, not secrets; each entry is a reviewed exemption
# scripts/licence-exceptions.txt — a reviewed licence decision

# Compiled service binaries. `go build ./cmd/...` drops these in the repo root; they are
# 25-40MB each and there is no reason for one to be committed. Build into ./bin via the
# Makefile instead.
/control-plane-api
/payment-api
/payment-orchestrator
/workflow-worker
/webhook-ingress
/outbox-relay
/event-consumer
/gateway-simulator
/platformctl
/bin/
